      <div class="two">
        <div class="prose">
          <p>I'm a quantitative trader on the Index Options team at Optiver's Mumbai office — building and running strategies where math, markets, and machines converge every day.</p>
          <p>I studied Computer Science at IIT Delhi (class of 2025). Along the way I interned at Jane Street in Hong Kong and Optiver in Amsterdam — two experiences that made it clear where I wanted to be. Each pushed me further into the intersection I find most interesting: the point where financial theory gets hard, computation gets real, and abstraction meets consequence.</p>
          <p>Outside of work, I'm thinking about AI — not just as a tool, but as a field with deep theoretical roots worth understanding from the ground up. I like building things, reading, and occasionally writing down thoughts that feel worth sharing. This site is the library those habits produce.</p>
          <p>Three things I'm made of, in the order they happened: olympiad mathematics, live risk on a trading desk, and — for the last year — running frontier models as agents on real problems, every day. The library exists because the fourth thing, whatever it is, will be learned the same way: from the ground floor, in public.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="pull">It's hard to do a really good job on anything you don't think about in the shower.<small>Paul Graham — it ended up on my CV for a reason</small></div>
